eference_comparison\",\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"purpose\": \"Compare measured one-shot library, split-cap averaging, and structure-aware outputs within each final dataset/model condition without pooling away reference-quality differences.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"grouped_dot\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n    \"group_by\": \"coalition_cap\",\n    \"metric\": \"normalized L1 reference agreement = 1/(1 + ||phi-phi_ref||_1/max(||phi_ref||_1,0.001))\",\n    \"split_by\": \"dataset x classifier, with exhaustive versus approximate reference stated in each panel\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"At 5.5in full text width, a 2x2 grid gives approximately 2.6in per panel; three short cap labels and three method series fit with 9pt labels and one shared legend. Target approximately 3.5\\u20134in height plus caption (about 0.48 page). A hypothetical half-width placement would make four panels unreadable. Use a common 0\\u20131 agreement axis and explicit numeric annotations or the companion table for ceiling-level differences, not a concealed truncated scale.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 4,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 2,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"min_rendered_font_pt\": 9,\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n      \"final.metric.reference_fidelity\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"figure_id\": \"component_comparison\",\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"purpose\": \"Test whether the observed development-data differences localize to the forest and logistic components rather than presenting configuration order as evidence.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"paired_dot\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n    \"group_by\": \"dataset_and_coalition_cap\",\n    \"metric\": \"normalized L1 reference agreement, using the same definition as the final comparison\",\n    \"split_by\": \"forest component and logistic component, explicitly development data\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"Two side-by-side panels at 5.5in full text width, approximately 2.2\\u20132.5in high plus caption (about 0.32 page). Each has four abbreviated dataset/cap categories and two configuration series, with the two episode points shown rather than invented standard errors. Keep 9pt labels and explanatory full labels in the caption; simplify rather than shrink. Do not add an ordering axis or arrows between configurations.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 2,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 2,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 4,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 2,\n    \"min_rendered_font_pt\": 9,\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"result.top_program_01\",\n      \"result.top_program_02\",\n      \"result.top_program_03\"\n    ]\n  }\n]\nREFS 25\nREF EXAMPLE {'citation_count': 45529, 'citation_key': 'Lundberg2017AUA', 'id': 'ref.s2.442e10a3c6640ded9408622005e3c2a8906ce4c2', 'paper_id': '442e10a3c6640ded9408622005e3c2a8906ce4c2', 'query': '\"A Unified Approach to Interpreting Model Predictions\" Lundberg Lee', 'retrieved_at': '2026-11-07T03:44:12.066927+00:00', 'source_url': 'https://api.semanticscholar.org/graph/v1/paper/442e10a3c6640ded9408622005e3c2a8906ce4c2?fields=paperId%2Ctitle%2Cyear%2Cvenue%2CcitationCount%2CcitationStyles%2Curl', 'title': 'A Unified Approach to Interpreting Model Predictions', 'venue': 'Neural Information Processing Systems', 'year': 2017}\nPROGRAMS [(dict_keys(['attempt_dir_name', 'attempt_id', 'combined_score', 'correct', 'eligible', 'eval_index', 'evaluation_evidence', 'idea_dir_name', 'idea_id', 'program_dir', 'program_id', 'program_idx']), 'work/results/t03/codex/20261107_013849/investigation/ideas/01_fixed_budget_single_call_shap_certificates/program_1'), (dict_keys(['attempt_dir_name', 'attempt_id', 'combined_score', 'correct', 'eligible', 'eval_