{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_106","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'apply_patch() { codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch \"$(cat)\"; }\napply_patch <<'\"'PATCH'\n*** Add File: REPRODUCIBILITY.md\n+# Reproducing the fixed-game SHAP study\n+\n+## What is measured\n+\n+\"'`paper_data.json` is the immutable measurement registry. The final evaluation is completed and qualified according to `final.qualification.*`; this is an execution/integrity/control outcome, not evidence of deployment validity. The main paper uses final episodes independently of development selection. There is no downstream-study object or additional task list in this registry. German Credit and ACSIncome-2024-RELSHIPP each have logistic and forest conditions. No new training, attribution experiment, or evaluator execution was performed during writing.\n+\n+## Files and source evidence\n+\n+- `source_evidence/selected/`: retained structure-aware estimator, dispatch, response interface, and independent validation routines.\n+- `source_evidence/sampled/`: custom sampled comparison implementation.\n+- `source_evidence/forest/`: forest component comparison implementation.\n+- `source_evidence/evaluation/`: final/development evaluators, acquisition code, pinned requirements and data provenance.\n+- `task/resources/{search,final}/`: frozen records and original provenance, accessible through the supplied task link.\n+- `analysis_summary.json`: descriptive reductions of recorded observations, not additional experiments.\n+- `claims_grounding.json`: claim-to-registry mapping plus readable source locations.\n+- `scientific-evidence/`: evidence grammar, schemas, and verification report.\n+\n+`source_evidence/MANIFEST.json` records hashes of the copied evidence. These identify provenance only; implementation claims require reading the files. The independent validation routines are included but have no recorded executions in the research evidence. Do not count them as empirical controls.\n+\n+## Recorded scientific environment\n+\n+Python 3.12.15 is available in the supplied scientific environment. The preserved requirements include NumPy 2.1.3, SciPy 1.15.3, scikit-learn 1.6.1, SHAP 0.48.0, pandas 2.2.3 and folktables 0.0.12. See the full pinned file rather than treating this short list as a complete environment lock. Dependency metadata for those six libraries was inspected during writing; a fresh installation of the entire lock was not tested.\n+\n+For a new installation, create a private environment outside the manuscript workspace:\n+\n+```sh\n+python3.12 -m venv /tmp/shap-study-env\n+/tmp/shap-study-env/bin/pip install -r source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt\n+```\n+\n+The evaluation uses Linux process isolation, CPU affinity, Landlock/seccomp, and bounded memory. A non-Linux port of the evaluator was not tested. BLAS thread limits are set in the evaluator; forest fitting uses one thread. The source-task compute estimate is not a measured CPU ledger.\n+\n+## Public data and recapture\n+\n+Exact download URLs, digests, terms, release metadata and content-normalization conventions are in `source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json`. German data are UCI Statlog German Credit, DOI 10.24432/C5NC77, under CC BY 4.0. ACS uses the actual 2024 one-year CA and NY PUMS releases, with the release-specific `RELSHIPP` field replacing absent historical `RELP`. Do not describe the result as unmodified historical ACSIncome. The original acquisition excludes cross-state raw predictor-content overlaps before selecting retained data. It keeps one representative per predictor-content group and records duplicate/conflicting-label provenance.\n+\n+For offline reproduction, use the supplied frozen `task/resources` files. For an independent recapture, download each `sources[*].url` to `/tmp/public-source/<sources[*].file>`, verify its recorded SHA256, then run:\n+\n+```sh\n+python source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py '\"\\\\\n+  --source_dir /tmp/public-source --output_root /tmp/new-resources\n+\"'```\n+\n+No recapture or new data download was performed during paper writing. Retaining matching public archives is the reproducibility route if an upstream release later changes. The frozen resources suffice for offline evaluation.\n+\n+## Evaluation commands (documented, not rerun during writing)\n+\n+```sh\n+TASK_SOURCE_DIR=\"$PWD/task\" /tmp/shap-study-env/bin/python '\"\\\\\n+  source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py \\\\\n+  --program_path \\\"\"'$PWD/source_evidence/selected/program.py\" '\"\\\\\n+  --results_dir /tmp/shap-final-reproduction\n+\"'```\n+\n+Final episode seeds are 104729, 130363 and 155921. Coalition caps are 64, 256 and 1024, with six repeated calls and sixteen fixed queries/background rows per fitted condition. Development seeds are 1729 and 2718, caps 64 and 256, eight queries, and four repeats. The evaluator source supplies model, reference, baseline, reset and replay details. The recorded full final evaluation wall total is 700.3707705293782 seconds, including comparators and references; this is an observed workload duration, not a guaranteed runtime or candidate latency. The evaluator enforces a larger wall limit; no CPU-hour usage estimate is reconstructed.\n+\n+## Figures and tables\n+\n+Rendering tools are installed in a separate private environment. The writing run used `/tmp/paper-tools`; no package tree or environment symlink is placed in the manuscript workspace.\n+\n+```sh\n+python -m venv /tmp/paper-tools\n+/tmp/paper-tools/bin/pip install numpy matplotlib pillow jsonschema pypdf requests Unidecode\n+/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python build_artifacts.py\n+```\n+\n+- Figure `final_reference_comparison`: final non-replay candidate cells and `observations.baseline_metrics`, grouped by dataset/model and cap.\n+- Figure `component_comparison`: matched development episode cells for the forest and logistic components. This is not final held-out evidence.\n+- Figure `reference_diagnostics`: final German candidate/reference L1 distances and the recorded reference half-difference proxy.\n+- All numerical tables: `build_artifacts.py`, with fragments under `tables/`. For a self-contained supplementary section, the manuscript embeds the generated rows directly rather than importing them. Regeneration updates the fragments; changes to measured inputs would require an explicitly audited manuscript revision, not silent substitution.\n+- Figure `fixed_game_overview`: orchestrator-owned conceptual render. Its guarded placeholder and empty plan stub are intentionally replaced synchronously after this writing step. The script never overwrites a completed render. This diagram contains no fabricated measured results.\n+\n+Quantitative plots export PDF and 300-DPI PNG. LaTeX includes PDFs. The full text width is 5.5 inches, with at least nine-point plotted labels at that width. Adjacent `.prov.json` sidecars connect derived outputs to real input files. The final sign metric blends reference and repeat comparisons in the evaluator; the paper instead reports the pure reference-cell mean and explains the distinction.\n+\n+## Manuscript, references and checks\n+\n+The manuscript uses the official ICLR 2026 style and bibliography style retrieved from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ICLR/Master-Template/master/iclr2026.zip`, retained under `template_evidence/` and copied to `paper.sty` / `paper.bst`. It uses the anonymous review mode. `VENUE.md` fixes the target year despite the template repository containing other years.\n+\n+`curate_references.py` selects known permitted primary works by DOI or exact title through OpenAlex. Semantic Scholar was rate-limited. Bibliographic records and available abstracts were read; references/citing-work graphs were not traversed. `literature_evidence/` preserves the selected records. An incorrect initial Owen DOI resolved to unrelated tuberculosis metadata; that metadata was immediately rejected, not cited, and the DOI was corrected to *Multilinear Extensions of Games*. No prohibited study was identified or deliberately sought. Earlier broad retrieval noise was removed, not cited as read literature. Absence of an identified encounter is not proof that earlier stages independently audited all retrieval noise.\n+\n+Standard compilation is:\n+\n+```sh\n+pdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n+bibtex paper\n+pdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n+pdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n+```\n+\n+The supplied skill validators check sections/citations, grounded claims, figure manifests, evidence references, and rendered supplementary information. The final `writing_validation.json` distinguishes completed checks from environment limitations and the pending orchestrator-owned diagram. Never interpret that pending render as a completed figure audit.\n+\n+## Interpretation limits\n+\n+The query-bootstrap intervals condition on fixed fitted models, queries and references and do not capture background choice or reference bias. German references are approximate; ACS references enumerate the finite game. Repeated pairs share queries. Structural parameter access differs from prediction-only access, and there is no equal-time comparison. No deployment, causal, human, background-shift or new-population validity claim is supported. LLM roles are disclosed in the manuscript.\n*** Add File: build_claims.py\n+import hashlib\n+import json\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+\n+def main():\n+    data = json.loads(Path('\"'paper_data.json').read_text())\n+    summary = json.loads(Path('analysis_summary.json').read_text())\n+    claims = []\n+    final_sources = ['final.evidence.episodes']\n+    development_sources = ['result.top_program_01', 'result.top_program_02', 'result.top_program_03']\n+\n+    def add(claim, sources=None, refs=None, files=None, scope='final fixed-game evaluation'):\n+        claims.append({'claim': claim, 'source_ids': sources or final_sources, 'citation_keys': refs or [], 'evidence_refs': files or ['paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes'], 'scope': scope})\n+\n+    add('The final evaluation is completed and qualified; this outcome concerns documented execution, integrity, coverage and controls, not deployment validity.', ['final.qualification.status', 'final.qualification.outcome', 'final.qualification.correct'], files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1253-L1273'])\n+    add('Aggregate final normalized L1 reference agreement is 0.9975639445869278 (0.99756 in the abstract).', ['final.metric.reference_fidelity'])\n+    add('All final structure-aware reference top-three overlaps and repeat-pair top-three/sign agreements equal one; these are different assessments.', ['final.metric.top3_overlap', 'final.evidence.episodes'])\n+    add('Stored vectors have maximum coordinate range zero across repeats, conditional on each cap, model and fixed query.', files=['analysis_summary.json#/max_repeat_vector_difference', 'paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes'])\n+    add(f\\\"Pure final reference sign agreement is {summary['reference_sign_mean']:.10f}, distinct from the evaluator's mixed reference/repeat summary.\\\", ['final.evidence.episodes', 'final.metric.signed_agreement'], files=['analysis_summary.json#/reference_sign_mean', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1038-L1053'])\n+    add('Mean normalized endpoint residual is 1.27919753412707e-11; control pass rate is one, failed-call fraction zero, and replay error zero.', ['final.metric.efficiency_error', 'final.metric.control_pass_rate', 'final.metric.failed_fraction', 'final.metric.replay_error'])\n+    add('The full recorded final workload took 700.3707705293782 wall seconds (700.37 reported); references/comparators/training are included and candidate-only latency is unavailable.', ['final.metric.wall_seconds'], files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1310-L1343', 'paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics/wall_seconds'])\n+    add('There are four final dataset/model conditions: German logistic, German forest, ACS logistic and ACS forest. No additional task list or downstream-study comparison exists.', files=['paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes'])\n+    add('Final seeds are 104729, 130363 and 155921; caps are 64, 256 and 1024; six calls per cap use sixteen fixed queries and sixteen training-background rows.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L34-L36', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1316-L1319', 'paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes'])\n+    add('Final German splits contain 300/100/100 retained records and twenty groups; ACS splits contain 20000/6667/6667 and ten groups. These are resource/protocol counts, not independent explained-sample counts.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L61-L155', 'source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L687-L718'])\n+    add('German targets use original class code 2. ACS uses 2024 PUMS, native RELSHIPP without a fabricated RELP crosswalk, the retained adult filter and PINCP greater than 50000 target.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L72-L155', 'source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json'], refs=['GermanCredit', 'Ding2021'])\n+    add('German development/final content groups are disjoint; ACS development uses California, final uses New York, with cross-state predictor-content intersections removed.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L72-L155', 'source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json'])\n+    add('Categorical ordinal encodings, unseen code -1, numeric medians, and standardization are training fitted; sixteen query/background rows are selected by fixed ordering.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L687-L718', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L838-L842'])\n+    add('Logistic regression uses lbfgs, max_iter 500 and tolerance 1e-7; forests have sixty-four trees, depth six and n_jobs one.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L833-L837'])\n+    add('ACS references enumerate the ten-feature finite game; German references average two independent cap-4096 library estimates. Half-differences are proxies, not calibrated intervals.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L774-L796', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L849-L858'])\n+    add('Stored 95-percent intervals use 1000 bootstrap resamples of sixteen query-level means after cap/repeat averaging, conditional on one fitted model/reference.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1154-L1159'], refs=['Efron1979'])\n+    add('The fixed-game normalized L1 score uses a norm floor of 0.001; signs at magnitudes at most 1e-8 are zero; top-three ties follow coordinate order.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1014-L1030'])\n+    add('Library comparison uses identity-link KernelExplainer with l1_reg zero and nsamples equal to cap. Two-start averaging gives each independent call floor(cap/2).', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L757-L772', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L860-L868'], refs=['Lundberg2017'])\n+    add('Forest attribution sums signed leaf-literal beta-integral coefficients across all background rows and trees; repeated splits are intersected and float32 predictor input semantics retained.', files=['source_evidence/selected/forest.py#L11-L81', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L720-L755'], refs=['Lundberg2018', 'Owen1972'])\n+    add('Logistic integration is on the probability game, uses ceil(d/2) inclusion nodes, eight-node frequency panels, cutoff eight and at most 2048 frequency nodes; tolerances are 1e-10 for tail and 1e-8 for mesh/efficiency.', files=['source_evidence/selected/logistic_fourier.py#L12-L140'])\n+    add('Two consecutive mesh agreements are required; numerical failure in any background row rejects all integration. Frequency-tail control is not a rigorous discretization bound.', files=['source_evidence/selected/logistic_fourier.py#L43-L140'])\n+    add('Dispatch uses forests directly and generic exhaustive calculation when cap covers 2\"'^d minus two nontrivial coalitions before considering logistic integration; branch counts are unrecorded.'\"', files=['source_evidence/selected/reliability.py#L163-L197'])\n+    add('The fallback uses independent complete paths and importance-corrected kernel regression. The internal simultaneous path radius at alpha 0.05 is used only with at least two paths; no acceptance coverage is established.', files=['source_evidence/selected/reliability.py#L66-L197'], refs=['Maurer2009','Hoeffding1963'])\n+    add('German reference half-difference mean absolute coordinates are about 1.05e-4 logistic and 1.20e-4 forest; no error decomposition follows.', files=['analysis_summary.json#/reference_uncertainty'])\n+    add('Seed-104729 query-bootstrap intervals round to [0.99618,0.99709] for German logistic and [0.99292,0.99442] for German forests.', files=['paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/cases/0/observations/fidelity_instance_bootstrap_ci95', 'paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/cases/1/observations/fidelity_instance_bootstrap_ci95'])\n+    add('At cap 64 the structure-aware versus library differences favor structure-aware agreement in all four retained final conditions; at cap 1024 both ACS library means round to one. This is not equal-time superiority.', files=['analysis_summary.json#/final'])\n+    add('At German cap 64 split-cap means round to 0.3341 logistic and 0.2995 forest, recovering to 0.9699 and 0.9448 at cap 256. The cause is not localized by recorded diagnostics.', files=['analysis_summary.json#/final'])\n+    add('Development comparisons use seeds 1729 and 2718, caps 64/256, eight queries and four repeats; their role is supporting component comparison, not held-out confirmation.', development_sources, files=['paper_data.json#/all_programs', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate.py#L1316-L1319'], scope='development only')\n+    add('Development German forest cap-64 changes from 0.858--0.870 to 0.9924--0.9929; German logistic changes from 0.946--0.951 to about 0.9963 with integration.', development_sources, files=['analysis_summary.json#/development'], scope='development only')\n+    add('Custom sampled development mean agreement is nonmonotone: ACS forest about 0.9674 to 0.9512 and German logistic about 0.9488 to 0.9137 from cap 64 to 256; no unique cause is established.', development_sources, files=['analysis_summary.json#/development'], scope='development only')\n+    add('Final validation accuracy is 0.67 German logistic, 0.65--0.69 German forests, about 0.7609 ACS logistic and 0.7755--0.7773 ACS forests; converged logistic fits record 19 and 13 iterations respectively.', files=['paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes'])\n+    add('Recorded scientific dependencies include NumPy 2.1.3, SciPy 1.15.3, scikit-learn 1.6.1, SHAP 0.48.0, pandas 2.2.3 and folktables 0.0.12; a fresh lock installation was not tested.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt'], refs=['Harris2020','Virtanen2020','Pedregosa2011','McKinney2010'])\n+    add('Written independent validation routines have no retained execution records and are not additional empirical evidence.', files=['source_evidence/selected/validate_forest.py','source_evidence/selected/validate_logistic_fourier.py'], scope='source inspection only')\n+    for row in summary['final']:\n+        add(f\\\"Final table seed {row['seed']}, {row['case']}, cap {row['cap']}: mean reference agreement library {row['standard'][0]:.10f}, split-cap {row['multistart'][0]:.10f}, structure-aware {row['structure'][0]:.10f}; structure-aware reference sign agreement {row['structure'][2]:.10f}; repeat top-three/sign means {row['repeat']}; stored query CI {row['bootstrap_ci95']}.\\\", files=['analysis_summary.json#/final', 'paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes'])\n+    for row in summary['development']:\n+        source = ['result.top_program_03', 'result.top_program_02', 'result.top_program_01'][row['configuration']]\n+        add(f\\\"Development component figure: configuration {row['configuration']}, seed {row['seed']}, {row['case']}, cap {row['cap']}: mean reference agreement {row['agreement']:.10f}.\\\", [source], files=['analysis_summary.json#/development','paper_data.json#/all_programs'], scope='development only')\n+    for reference in json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())['references']:\n+        add('Bibliographic context: ' + reference['title'] + '. Only the relevant stated framing or software/data identity is used; it is not an evaluated comparator.', [reference['id']], refs=[reference['citation_key']], files=[reference['local_record']], scope='literature context')\n+    Path('claims_grounding.json').write_text(json.dumps({'claims': claims, 'interpretation_policy': 'Qualification is read independently of selection; no final failure is present. Metrics do not establish deployment validity. Readable code locations supply implementation support; registry IDs alone do not establish source identity. All reductions preserve final/development separation.'}, indent=2))\n+    files = sorted(Path('source_evidence').rglob('*'))\n+    manifest = {'files': [{'path': str(path), 'sha256': hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()} for path in files if path.is_file() and path.name \"'!= '\"'MANIFEST.json']}\n+    Path('source_evidence/MANIFEST.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest, indent=2))\n+    derived = ['@evidence[[paper_data.json]]', '@evidence[[analysis_summary.json]]', '@evidence[[references_provenance.json]]', '@evidence[[source_evidence/MANIFEST.json]]']\n+    for file, kind in [('claims_grounding.json','derived'), ('paper.tex','manuscript')]:\n+        provenance = {'schema_name': 'scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest', 'artifact': {'path': file, 'kind': kind, 'sha256': hashlib.sha256(Path(file).read_bytes()).hexdigest()}, 'derived_from': derived, 'generated_by': {'script_path': 'build_claims.py'}}\n+        Path(file + '.prov.json').write_text(json.dumps(provenance, indent=2))\n+    print('Wrote', len(claims), 'grounded claims')\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == '__main__':\n+    main()\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python build_claims.py\npython .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_106","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'apply_patch() { codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch \"$(cat)\"; }\napply_patch <<'\"'PATCH'\n*** Add File: REPRODUCIBILITY.md\n+# Reproducing the fixed-game SHAP study\n+\n+## What is measured\n+\n+\"'`paper_data.json` is the immutable measurement registry. The final evaluation is completed and qualified according to `final.qualification.*`; this is an execution/integrity/control outcome, not evidence of deployment validity. The main paper uses final episodes independently of development selection. There is no downstream-study object or additional task list in this registry. German Credit and ACSIncome-2024-RELSHIPP each have logistic and forest conditions. No new training, attribution experiment, or evaluator execution was performed during writing.\n+\n+## Files and source evidence\n+\n+- `source_evidence/selected/`: retained structure-aware estimator, dispatch, response interface, and independent validation routines.\n+- `source_evidence/sampled/`: custom sampled comparison implementation.\n+- `source_evidence/forest/`: forest component comparison implementation.\n+- `source_evidence/evaluation/`: final/development evaluators, acquisition code, pinned requirements and data provenance.\n+- `task/resources/{search,final}/`: frozen records and original provenance, accessible through the supplied task link.\n+- `analysis_summary.json`: descriptive reductions of recorded observations, not additional experiments.\n+- `claims_grounding.json`: claim-to-registry mapping plus readable source locations.\n+- `scientific-evidence/`: evidence grammar, schemas, and verification report.\n+\n+`source_evidence/MANIFEST.json` records hashes of the copied evidence. These identify provenance only; implementation claims require reading the files. The independent validation routines are included but have no recorded executions in the research evidence. Do not count them as empirical controls.\n+\n+## Recorded scientific environment\n+\n+Python 3.12.15 is available in the supplied scientific environment. The preserved requirements include NumPy 2.1.3, SciPy 1.15.3, scikit-learn 1.6.1, SHAP 0.48.0, pandas 2.2.3 and folktables 0.0.12. See the full pinned file rather than treating this short list as a complete environment lock. Dependency metadata for those six libraries was inspected during writing; a fresh installation of the entire lock was not tested.\n+\n+For a new installation, create a private environment outside the manuscript workspace:\n+\n+```sh\n+python3.12 -m venv /tmp/shap-study-env\n+/tmp/shap-study-env/bin/pip install -r source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt\n+```\n+\n+The evaluation uses Linux process isolation, CPU affinity, Landlock/seccomp, and bounded memory. A non-Linux port of the evaluator was not tested. BLAS thread limits are set in the evaluator; forest fitting uses one thread. The source-task compute estimate is not a measured CPU ledger.\n+\n+## Public data and recapture\n+\n+Exact download URLs, digests, terms, release metadata and content-normalization conventions are in `source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json`. German data are UCI Statlog German Credit, DOI 10.24432/C5NC77, under CC BY 4.0. ACS uses the actual 2024 one-year CA and NY PUMS releases, with the release-specific `RELSHIPP` field replacing absent historical `RELP`. Do not describe the result as unmodified historical ACSIncome. The original acquisition excludes cross-state raw predictor-content overlaps before selecting retained data. It keeps one representative per predictor-content group and records duplicate/conflicting-label provenance.\n+\n+For offline reproduction, use the supplied frozen `task/resources` files. For an independent recapture, download each `sources[*].url` to `/tmp/public-source/<sources[*].file>`, verify its recorded SHA256, then run:\n+\n+```sh\n+python source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py '\"\\\\\n+  --source_dir /tmp/public-source --output_root /tmp/new-resources\n+\"'```\n+\n+No recapture or new data download was performed during paper writing. Retaining matching public archives is the reproducibility route if an upstream release later changes. The frozen resources suffice for offline evaluation.\n+\n+## Evaluation commands (documented, not rerun during writing)\n+\n+```sh\n+TASK_SOURCE_DIR=\"$PWD/task\" /tmp/shap-study-env/bin/python '\"\\\\\n+  source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py \\\\\n+  --program_path \\\"\"'$PWD/source_evidence/selected/program.py\" '\"\\\\\n+  --results_dir /tmp/shap-final-reproduction\n+\"'```\n+\n+Final episode seeds are 104729, 130363 and 155921. Coalition caps are 64, 256 and 1024, with six repeated calls and sixteen fixed queries/background rows per fitted condition. Development seeds are 1729 and 2718, caps 64 and 256, eight queries, and four repeats. The evaluator source supplies model, reference, baseline, reset and replay details. The recorded full final evaluation wall total is 700.3707705293782 seconds, including comparators and references; this is an observed workload duration, not a guaranteed runtime or candidate latency. The evaluator enforces a larger wall limit; no CPU-hour usage estimate is reconstructed.\n+\n+## Figures and tables\n+\n+Rendering tools are installed in a separate private environment. The writing run used `/tmp/paper-tools`; no package tree or environment symlink is placed in the manuscript workspace.\n+\n+```sh\n+python -m venv /tmp/paper-tools\n+/tmp/paper-tools/bin/pip install numpy matplotlib pillow jsonschema pypdf requests Unidecode\n+/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python build_artifacts.py\n+```\n+\n+- Figure `final_reference_comparison`: final non-replay candidate cells and `observations.baseline_metrics`, grouped by dataset/model and cap.\n+- Figure `component_comparison`: matched development episode cells for the forest and logistic components. This is not final held-out evidence.\n+- Figure `reference_diagnostics`: final German candidate/reference L1 distances and the recorded reference half-difference proxy.\n+- All numerical tables: `build_artifacts.py`, with fragments under `tables/`. For a self-contained supplementary section, the manuscript embeds the generated rows directly rather than importing them. Regeneration updates the fragments; changes to measured inputs would require an explicitly audited manuscript revision, not silent substitution.\n+- Figure `fixed_game_overview`: orchestrator-owned conceptual render. Its guarded placeholder and empty plan stub are intentionally replaced synchronously after this writing step. The script never overwrites a completed render. This diagram contains no fabricated measured results.\n+\n+Quantitative plots export PDF and 300-DPI PNG. LaTeX includes PDFs. The full text width is 5.5 inches, with at least nine-point plotted labels at that width. Adjacent `.prov.json` sidecars connect derived outputs to real input files. The final sign metric blends reference and repeat comparisons in the evaluator; the paper instead reports the pure reference-cell mean and explains the distinction.\n+\n+## Manuscript, references and checks\n+\n+The manuscript uses the official ICLR 2026 style and bibliography style retrieved from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ICLR/Master-Template/master/iclr2026.zip`, retained under `template_evidence/` and copied to `paper.sty` / `paper.bst`. It uses the anonymous review mode. `VENUE.md` fixes the target year despite the template repository containing other years.\n+\n+`curate_references.py` selects known permitted primary works by DOI or exact title through OpenAlex. Semantic Scholar was rate-limited. Bibliographic records and available abstracts were read; references/citing-work graphs were not traversed. `literature_evidence/` preserves the selected records. An incorrect initial Owen DOI resolved to unrelated tuberculosis metadata; that metadata was immediately rejected, not cited, and the DOI was corrected to *Multilinear Extensions of Games*. No prohibited study was identified or deliberately sought. Earlier broad retrieval noise was removed, not cited as read literature. Absence of an identified encounter is not proof that earlier stages independently audited all retrieval noise.\n+\n+Standard compilation is:\n+\n+```sh\n+pdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n+bibtex paper\n+pdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n+pdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n+```\n+\n+The supplied skill validators check sections/citations, grounded claims, figure manifests, evidence references, and rendered supplementary information. The final `writing_validation.json` distinguishes completed checks from environment limitations and the pending orchestrator-owned diagram. Never interpret that pending render as a completed figure audit.\n+\n+## Interpretation limits\n+\n+The query-bootstrap intervals condition on fixed fitted models, queries and references and do not capture background choice or reference bias. German references are approximate; ACS references enumerate the finite game. Repeated pairs share queries. Structural parameter access differs from prediction-only access, and there is no equal-time comparison. No deployment, causal, human, background-shift or new-population validity claim is supported. LLM roles are disclosed in the manuscript.\n*** Add File: build_claims.py\n+import hashlib\n+import json\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+\n+def main():\n+    data = json.loads(Path('\"'paper_data.json').read_text())\n+    summary = json.loads(Path('analysis_summary.json').read_text())\n+    claims = []\n+    final_sources = ['final.evidence.episodes']\n+    development_sources = ['result.top_program_01', 'result.top_program_02', 'result.top_program_03']\n+\n+    def add(claim, sources=None, refs=None, files=None, scope='final fixed-game evaluation'):\n+        claims.append({'claim': claim, 'source_ids': sources or final_sources, 'citation_keys': refs or [], 'evidence_refs': files or ['paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes'], 'scope': scope})\n+\n+    add('The final evaluation is completed and qualified; this outcome concerns documented execution, integrity, coverage and controls, not deployment validity.', ['final.qualification.status', 'final.qualification.outcome', 'final.qualification.correct'], files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1253-L1273'])\n+    add('Aggregate final normalized L1 reference agreement is 0.9975639445869278 (0.99756 in the abstract).', ['final.metric.reference_fidelity'])\n+    add('All final structure-aware reference top-three overlaps and repeat-pair top-three/sign agreements equal one; these are different assessments.', ['final.metric.top3_overlap', 'final.evidence.episodes'])\n+    add('Stored vectors have maximum coordinate range zero across repeats, conditional on each cap, model and fixed query.', files=['analysis_summary.json#/max_repeat_vector_difference', 'paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes'])\n+    add(f\\\"Pure final reference sign agreement is {summary['reference_sign_mean']:.10f}, distinct from the evaluator's mixed reference/repeat summary.\\\", ['final.evidence.episodes', 'final.metric.signed_agreement'], files=['analysis_summary.json#/reference_sign_mean', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1038-L1053'])\n+    add('Mean normalized endpoint residual is 1.27919753412707e-11; control pass rate is one, failed-call fraction zero, and replay error zero.', ['final.metric.efficiency_error', 'final.metric.control_pass_rate', 'final.metric.failed_fraction', 'final.metric.replay_error'])\n+    add('The full recorded final workload took 700.3707705293782 wall seconds (700.37 reported); references/comparators/training are included and candidate-only latency is unavailable.', ['final.metric.wall_seconds'], files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1310-L1343', 'paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics/wall_seconds'])\n+    add('There are four final dataset/model conditions: German logistic, German forest, ACS logistic and ACS forest. No additional task list or downstream-study comparison exists.', files=['paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes'])\n+    add('Final seeds are 104729, 130363 and 155921; caps are 64, 256 and 1024; six calls per cap use sixteen fixed queries and sixteen training-background rows.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L34-L36', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1316-L1319', 'paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes'])\n+    add('Final German splits contain 300/100/100 retained records and twenty groups; ACS splits contain 20000/6667/6667 and ten groups. These are resource/protocol counts, not independent explained-sample counts.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L61-L155', 'source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L687-L718'])\n+    add('German targets use original class code 2. ACS uses 2024 PUMS, native RELSHIPP without a fabricated RELP crosswalk, the retained adult filter and PINCP greater than 50000 target.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L72-L155', 'source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json'], refs=['GermanCredit', 'Ding2021'])\n+    add('German development/final content groups are disjoint; ACS development uses California, final uses New York, with cross-state predictor-content intersections removed.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L72-L155', 'source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json'])\n+    add('Categorical ordinal encodings, unseen code -1, numeric medians, and standardization are training fitted; sixteen query/background rows are selected by fixed ordering.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L687-L718', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L838-L842'])\n+    add('Logistic regression uses lbfgs, max_iter 500 and tolerance 1e-7; forests have sixty-four trees, depth six and n_jobs one.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L833-L837'])\n+    add('ACS references enumerate the ten-feature finite game; German references average two independent cap-4096 library estimates. Half-differences are proxies, not calibrated intervals.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L774-L796', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L849-L858'])\n+    add('Stored 95-percent intervals use 1000 bootstrap resamples of sixteen query-level means after cap/repeat averaging, conditional on one fitted model/reference.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1154-L1159'], refs=['Efron1979'])\n+    add('The fixed-game normalized L1 score uses a norm floor of 0.001; signs at magnitudes at most 1e-8 are zero; top-three ties follow coordinate order.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1014-L1030'])\n+    add('Library comparison uses identity-link KernelExplainer with l1_reg zero and nsamples equal to cap. Two-start averaging gives each independent call floor(cap/2).', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L757-L772', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L860-L868'], refs=['Lundberg2017'])\n+    add('Forest attribution sums signed leaf-literal beta-integral coefficients across all background rows and trees; repeated splits are intersected and float32 predictor input semantics retained.', files=['source_evidence/selected/forest.py#L11-L81', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L720-L755'], refs=['Lundberg2018', 'Owen1972'])\n+    add('Logistic integration is on the probability game, uses ceil(d/2) inclusion nodes, eight-node frequency panels, cutoff eight and at most 2048 frequency nodes; tolerances are 1e-10 for tail and 1e-8 for mesh/efficiency.', files=['source_evidence/selected/logistic_fourier.py#L12-L140'])\n+    add('Two consecutive mesh agreements are required; numerical failure in any background row rejects all integration. Frequency-tail control is not a rigorous discretization bound.', files=['source_evidence/selected/logistic_fourier.py#L43-L140'])\n+    add('Dispatch uses forests directly and generic exhaustive calculation when cap covers 2\"'^d minus two nontrivial coalitions before considering logistic integration; branch counts are unrecorded.'\"', files=['source_evidence/selected/reliability.py#L163-L197'])\n+    add('The fallback uses independent complete paths and importance-corrected kernel regression. The internal simultaneous path radius at alpha 0.05 is used only with at least two paths; no acceptance coverage is established.', files=['source_evidence/selected/reliability.py#L66-L197'], refs=['Maurer2009','Hoeffding1963'])\n+    add('German reference half-difference mean absolute coordinates are about 1.05e-4 logistic and 1.20e-4 forest; no error decomposition follows.', files=['analysis_summary.json#/reference_uncertainty'])\n+    add('Seed-104729 query-bootstrap intervals round to [0.99618,0.99709] for German logistic and [0.99292,0.99442] for German forests.', files=['paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/cases/0/observations/fidelity_instance_bootstrap_ci95', 'paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/cases/1/observations/fidelity_instance_bootstrap_ci95'])\n+    add('At cap 64 the structure-aware versus library differences favor structure-aware agreement in all four retained final conditions; at cap 1024 both ACS library means round to one. This is not equal-time superiority.', files=['analysis_summary.json#/final'])\n+    add('At German cap 64 split-cap means round to 0.3341 logistic and 0.2995 forest, recovering to 0.9699 and 0.9448 at cap 256. The cause is not localized by recorded diagnostics.', files=['analysis_summary.json#/final'])\n+    add('Development comparisons use seeds 1729 and 2718, caps 64/256, eight queries and four repeats; their role is supporting component comparison, not held-out confirmation.', development_sources, files=['paper_data.json#/all_programs', 'source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate.py#L1316-L1319'], scope='development only')\n+    add('Development German forest cap-64 changes from 0.858--0.870 to 0.9924--0.9929; German logistic changes from 0.946--0.951 to about 0.9963 with integration.', development_sources, files=['analysis_summary.json#/development'], scope='development only')\n+    add('Custom sampled development mean agreement is nonmonotone: ACS forest about 0.9674 to 0.9512 and German logistic about 0.9488 to 0.9137 from cap 64 to 256; no unique cause is established.', development_sources, files=['analysis_summary.json#/development'], scope='development only')\n+    add('Final validation accuracy is 0.67 German logistic, 0.65--0.69 German forests, about 0.7609 ACS logistic and 0.7755--0.7773 ACS forests; converged logistic fits record 19 and 13 iterations respectively.', files=['paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes'])\n+    add('Recorded scientific dependencies include NumPy 2.1.3, SciPy 1.15.3, scikit-learn 1.6.1, SHAP 0.48.0, pandas 2.2.3 and folktables 0.0.12; a fresh lock installation was not tested.', files=['source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt'], refs=['Harris2020','Virtanen2020','Pedregosa2011','McKinney2010'])\n+    add('Written independent validation routines have no retained execution records and are not additional empirical evidence.', files=['source_evidence/selected/validate_forest.py','source_evidence/selected/validate_logistic_fourier.py'], scope='source inspection only')\n+    for row in summary['final']:\n+        add(f\\\"Final table seed {row['seed']}, {row['case']}, cap {row['cap']}: mean reference agreement library {row['standard'][0]:.10f}, split-cap {row['multistart'][0]:.10f}, structure-aware {row['structure'][0]:.10f}; structure-aware reference sign agreement {row['structure'][2]:.10f}; repeat top-three/sign means {row['repeat']}; stored query CI {row['bootstrap_ci95']}.\\\", files=['analysis_summary.json#/final', 'paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes'])\n+    for row in summary['development']:\n+        source = ['result.top_program_03', 'result.top_program_02', 'result.top_program_01'][row['configuration']]\n+        add(f\\\"Development component figure: configuration {row['configuration']}, seed {row['seed']}, {row['case']}, cap {row['cap']}: mean reference agreement {row['agreement']:.10f}.\\\", [source], files=['analysis_summary.json#/development','paper_data.json#/all_programs'], scope='development only')\n+    for reference in json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())['references']:\n+        add('Bibliographic context: ' + reference['title'] + '. Only the relevant stated framing or software/data identity is used; it is not an evaluated comparator.', [reference['id']], refs=[reference['citation_key']], files=[reference['local_record']], scope='literature context')\n+    Path('claims_grounding.json').write_text(json.dumps({'claims': claims, 'interpretation_policy': 'Qualification is read independently of selection; no final failure is present. Metrics do not establish deployment validity. Readable code locations supply implementation support; registry IDs alone do not establish source identity. All reductions preserve final/development separation.'}, indent=2))\n+    files = sorted(Path('source_evidence').rglob('*'))\n+    manifest = {'files': [{'path': str(path), 'sha256': hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()} for path in files if path.is_file() and path.name \"'!= '\"'MANIFEST.json']}\n+    Path('source_evidence/MANIFEST.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest, indent=2))\n+    derived = ['@evidence[[paper_data.json]]', '@evidence[[analysis_summary.json]]', '@evidence[[references_provenance.json]]', '@evidence[[source_evidence/MANIFEST.json]]']\n+    for file, kind in [('claims_grounding.json','derived'), ('paper.tex','manuscript')]:\n+        provenance = {'schema_name': 'scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest', 'artifact': {'path': file, 'kind': kind, 'sha256': hashlib.sha256(Path(file).read_bytes()).hexdigest()}, 'derived_from': derived, 'generated_by': {'script_path': 'build_claims.py'}}\n+        Path(file + '.prov.json').write_text(json.dumps(provenance, indent=2))\n+    print('Wrote', len(claims), 'grounded claims')\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == '__main__':\n+    main()\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python build_claims.py\npython .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .\"","aggregated_output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/workspace/paper/.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\", line 661, in <module>\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n                     ^^^^^^\n  File \"/workspace/paper/.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\", line 603, in main\n    claims = read_json(Path(args.claims))\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/workspace/paper/.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\", line 92, in read_json\n    payload = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/pathlib.py\", line 1027, in read_text\n    with self.open(mode='r', encoding=encoding, errors=errors) as f:\n         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/pathlib.py\", line 1013, in open\n    return io.open(self, mode, buffering, encoding, errors, newline)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'claims_grounding.json'\n",